  "circulation": "A pier ladder is never the only way out: wide supported deck returns run on both sides. Undercroft remains dry for the entire mission seed; rising-tide hazards cannot strand a player or remove the required extraction path.",
  "systems": "Tidal boundary, wave impacts, wet timber, cold storage and wind have stable baselines. Boat silhouettes are scenery with collision barriers, not undeclared transport. Safe van stays on land.",
  "campaign": "Logbooks at fish house and cottage, storm records in boathouse. A shipment record can link Greywater Cannery while contradicting departure dates.",
  "refine": [
    "Refine support piles, edge rails, guard openings and at least 2 m clear deck paths; diagrams show deck envelopes.",
    "Choose and lock tide envelope before mission start; no required wading.",
    "Research working-wharf and fish-house construction before detailed shell authoring."
  ],
